+## Experimental executable contract preparation
+
+During criteria preparation, when project capabilities support inexpensive executable checks, the lead writes a small project-specific contract suite before implementing the behavior. Choose observable valid and invalid outcomes from the frozen requirements. Run the suite against the initial project and retain the actual result; an unavailable implementation proves only that the implementation is absent, not that the assertions are adequate or that a product regressed. The independent reviewer challenges the cases and their expected outcomes during the existing design challenge before implementation.
+
+Freeze the reviewed contract bytes. Implement the requested behavior and rerun those same checks. Record the before/after observations and suite identity. Any necessary contract amendment needs a reasoned criteria amendment and fresh independent criticism; a failed implementation does not justify weakening assertions. Preserve all ordinary independent behavioral verification, exact-source review, evidence freshness and acceptance requirements. This experimental preparation step changes no stage ownership or acceptance gate and claims no measured efficiency benefit without a controlled trial.
 
